  "candidate_or_production_modified": false,
  "conclusion": "The selector is equivalent to the serial greedy selector under the reviewed static eligibility contract, by a strict-total-order decomposition at N21 and N24. Two large direct composed miters timed out and remain unknown.",
  "scope": [
    "Actual CPU_ORDER_FUNCTION copied verbatim: arbitrary unsigned ages including ties and out-of-range values; stable order is (age,original slot).",
    "Actual CPU_RANK_FUNCTION copied verbatim: every output row checked against serial integer counting for an unconstrained older matrix and arbitrary valid mask. Rank correctness is proved, not assumed.",
    "Canonical strict-order actual-rank selector versus serial greedy at N21/N24, WB and IQ widths1/2/4; arbitrary ready/class/enable, all free-lane holes, MDU occupied/mul-ready/div-ready/div-accepted controls. Memory cap2 and MDU cap1.",
    "Strict total orders are reduced by relabeling candidates in priority order. Permuting rows/columns preserves proven counts and selected identities. The same one-hot winners imply the same masked-OR data/index outputs.",
    "Direct unsorted compositions at N5 widths1/2/4, N21 WB1, IQ1/IQ2 width4, and minimal ROB4 IQ1/IQ2/WB6 width4. All ages are unconstrained; strict sentinel is ROB_ENTRIES+1."
  ],
  "source_review": [
    "Operand ready bits, iq_live, address_ready, wait readiness and ages do not change between selection lanes. Existing MDU occupancy/accepted-DIV gating is identical.",
    "The old selection changes only selected-entry availability and the MEM/MDU issue counters. A selected load gains address_sent; a data-ready store becomes invalid; a data-unready store gains address_sent and remains data-unready, so it cannot be selected twice. Other instructions become invalid.",
    "Class-prefix filtering is independent of which free lane consumes a winner. Port rank increments only for a free lane within ISSUE_WIDTH."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Combinational selection equivalence, not whole-core sequential equivalence. Eligibility mutation invariants are established by source review, not a full pipeline SAT model.",
    "The full N21 WB4 and N24 IQ4 unsorted miters each reached the 60-second process limit. These are unknown, not direct passes.",
    "Age-width cases imply ROB32 for six-bit ages and ROB4 for three-bit ages. No non-power-of-two ROB sentinel was separately instantiated."
  ],
